---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../../data/site';

const updated = 'August 23, 2026';
const contact = site.contactEmail;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cuddle Crush — Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of Service for Cuddle Crush, Squish ’Em, published by MonkeyPayPay."
>
  <article class="prose legal container">
    <a class="app__back" href="/#flagship">← Cuddle Crush</a>
    <h1>Cuddle Crush, Squish ’Em — Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal__meta">Published by MonkeyPayPay · Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are a contract between you and MonkeyPayPay (“we”, “us”) covering Cuddle Crush,
      Squish ’Em (“the Game”). By installing or playing the Game you accept them. If you do not
      accept them, do not play.
    </p>
    <p>Our Privacy Policy explains what we do with your data and forms part of these Terms.</p>

    <h2>2. Who may play</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the Game if you are old enough to form a binding contract where you live, or if a
      parent or guardian agrees to these Terms on your behalf and supervises your use.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some features carry their own age limits. Shardfall staking requires you to be at least the
      minimum age shown in the Game and is unavailable otherwise.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Your account</h2>
    <p>You may play as a guest or register with an email address.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep your credentials to yourself. You are responsible for what happens on your account.</li>
      <li>One person, one account. Do not share, sell, buy or transfer accounts.</li>
      <li>
        Choose a display name that is not offensive, not impersonating someone, and not infringing
        anyone’s rights. We may change or reset a name that is.
      </li>
      <li>
        A guest account is not a backup. If you uninstall the Game without registering an email
        address, we may have no way to prove which guest account was yours, and progress may be
        unrecoverable.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can delete your account at any time from Account → Delete Account. It is immediate and
      permanent, and it destroys your progress and any unspent in-game currency, which is not
      refundable.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Licence</h2>
    <p>
      We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and play
      the Game for your own entertainment. We keep all other rights.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may not: copy, modify, decompile or reverse-engineer the Game except where law permits; use
      cheats, bots, automation, modified clients or exploits; interfere with our servers; scrape or
      bulk-collect data; or resell or commercially exploit any part of the Game.
    </p>

    <h2>5. In-game currencies and items</h2>
    <p>The Game has three currencies. They behave differently and it matters:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Coins</strong> — earned by playing. Cannot be bought.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Gems</strong> — bought with real money, and occasionally granted. Cosmetic and
        convenience purchases only.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Shards</strong> — earned by playing, and the only currency that can be staked in
        Shardfall. Shards cannot be purchased with money, and never will be.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>For all three, and for every fighter, skin, crystal and cosmetic:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>They are a limited licence to use a digital item inside the Game. You do not own them.</li>
      <li>
        They have no monetary value, cannot be exchanged for money or anything of real-world value,
        and cannot be transferred, sold or traded outside the Game.
      </li>
      <li>They may be changed, rebalanced, or discontinued as the Game develops.</li>
      <li>They are lost when your account is closed or deleted, by you or by us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>5.1 Shardfall staking is not gambling</h3>
    <p>
      Shardfall lets players stake Shards on a match, with the winner taking the pot. Shards are
      earned only. They cannot be bought with money, and they cannot be cashed out or converted into
      money or any item of real-world value. No real money enters or leaves this system in either
      direction.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Purchases, subscriptions and refunds</h2>
    <p>
      Purchases are processed by Apple or Google, not by us, under their terms. Prices are shown
      before you buy and include applicable taxes where required.
    </p>
    <p>
      Refunds are handled by Apple or Google, according to the policy of the store you bought from.
      Contact them, not us, in the first instance.
    </p>

    <h3>6.1 What happens when a purchase is refunded</h3>
    <p>When Apple or Google tells us a purchase was refunded, revoked or charged back, we reverse it:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The Gems that purchase granted are removed from your account.</li>
      <li>Any entitlement it bought — for example a Cuddle Club subscription term — ends.</li>
      <li>
        If you have already spent those Gems, your balance may go below zero. You are not billed for
        the difference and we will not pursue you for it, but you cannot make further in-game
        purchases until the balance returns to zero.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This exists so that buying, spending and then refunding is not a way to get items for free. It
      is not a penalty and there is no additional charge.
    </p>
    <p>We may also suspend an account that repeatedly buys and refunds.</p>

    <h3>6.2 Subscriptions</h3>
    <p>
      Cuddle Club renews automatically until cancelled. Cancel through your Apple or Google account
      settings; cancelling stops future renewals and does not refund the current term. Deleting the
      Game does not cancel a subscription.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Seasons, competition and rewards</h2>
    <p>
      The Game runs seasons. Ranks, leaderboards and seasonal rewards reset or are awarded at the end
      of each one.
    </p>
    <p>
      Champion Skins are awarded to the top players of each fighter at the close of a season.
      Rankings use a statistical confidence measure with a minimum number of matches played,
      deliberately, so that a single lucky result cannot win a board. Champion Skins are awarded only.
      They are never sold.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may adjust balance, rewards, matchmaking and season structure. Doing so is part of running a
      live game and is not a breach of these Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Fair play and conduct</h2>
    <p>Do not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>cheat, exploit bugs, use unauthorised software, or manipulate matchmaking;</li>
      <li>deliberately lose, collude, or arrange match outcomes, including in Shardfall;</li>
      <li>harass, threaten, bully or abuse other players;</li>
      <li>
        post hateful, sexual, violent or illegal content, including in crew chat or in a display
        name;
      </li>
      <li>impersonate anyone, including us;</li>
      <li>share another person’s private information.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Crew chat is not private. Every member of the crew can read it, and we may review messages that
      are reported to us.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you find a bug that gives an advantage, tell us. Exploiting it instead is a breach of these
      Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Suspension and termination</h2>
    <p>
      We may suspend or close an account that breaches these Terms. Where it is reasonable and the
      breach is not serious, we will warn first. For cheating, fraud, payment abuse or conduct that
      endangers other players, we may act immediately.
    </p>
    <p>Closing an account forfeits its progress and unspent currency without refund.</p>
    <p>You may stop playing and delete your account at any time.</p>

    <h2>10. Availability</h2>
    <p>
      The Game is an online service. It needs a connection, and it will sometimes be unavailable for
      maintenance, updates, or reasons outside our control. We do not guarantee uninterrupted
      availability, and we may change or discontinue features.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we ever shut the Game down permanently, we will give reasonable notice in the Game and stop
      selling Gems before we do.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Your content</h2>
    <p>
      Anything you submit — a display name, a chat message, a report, feedback — you grant us a
      worldwide, royalty-free licence to use for operating and improving the Game. You confirm you
      have the right to submit it. We may remove content that breaches section 8.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Disclaimers</h2>
    <p>
      The Game is provided “as is” and “as available”. To the fullest extent the law allows, we
      disclaim implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
      non-infringement.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing here limits your statutory consumer rights, which vary by country and which these Terms
      do not take away.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or
      consequential loss, or for lost progress, lost in-game items, or lost profits.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where liability cannot be excluded, it is limited to the greater of (a) the amount you paid us
      in the 12 months before the claim, or (b) USD 50.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not exclude liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud,
      or for anything else that cannot lawfully be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes to these Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms. Material changes will be announced in the Game before they take
      effect. Continuing to play after that means you accept them; if you do not, delete your
      account.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, USA, and the courts located in
      California have exclusive jurisdiction — except that if you are a consumer, you keep the
      protection of the mandatory laws of the country you live in, and may bring proceedings there.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Apple and Google</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are between you and us, not with Apple or Google. Neither is responsible for the
      Game or for support. Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms
      and may enforce them against you.
    </p>

    <h2>17. General</h2>
    <p>
      If any provision is unenforceable, the rest stands. Not enforcing a right immediately does not
      waive it. You may not assign these Terms; we may assign them to a successor of our business.
    </p>

    <h2>18. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      MonkeyPayPay — <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>
      <br />
      <span class="todo">[POSTAL ADDRESS — optional; add before launch if you want one listed]</span>
    </p>

    <hr />
    <p class="legal__note">
      Questions about these Terms? Contact <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. See also the{' '}
      <a href="/games/cuddle-crush/privacy">Cuddle Crush Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal .todo {
    background: rgba(255, 176, 32, 0.16);
    color: #ffca6a;
    border: 1px dashed rgba(255, 176, 32, 0.5);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0 0.35em;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }
  .legal h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
  }
</style>
